[list]
[*]Rival Exchanges are separate from diplomatic rivalries again. Your Exchange rivals whichever Exchanges it likes, as many as it likes. A rivalry counts whichever side started it.
[*]Each rival costs influence maintenance by its Standing, from 25 to 150, like vanilla pacts. Rivaling costs 10 relations at once, then 1 a month down to Poor. A rivalry cannot be ended in its first year.
[*]The Leading Exchanges list has a rivalry button on each Exchange, in the style of vanilla's subsidize button: a silhouette while off, lit while you rival them. Its tooltip gives the maintenance and the relations cost. A small shield marks Exchanges that rival you.
[*]Rivalries are now a tug of war settled every 5 years. The bar starts from the two scores, and each action that works pushes it 10% your way, up to 5 pushes a side. It settles in five results: a draw near the middle, a win that takes trust from the loser, or a decisive win that takes twice as much plus 10% of the loser's investment pool income for a year.
[*]The Rivalries section has two tables with one layout: Country, Contest (the tug-of-war bar, with ticks for the results), Effects (actions running on them, with months left) and Actions. You can act against Exchanges rivaling you too. Your own row shows when the contest settles, and Shore Up.
[*]New action Hold the Line undoes one of a rival's pushes against you.
[*]New icons for the rival moves, a painted picture for the rival event, and a new Speculative Excess alert icon.
[*]AI Exchanges rival the nearest-scoring Exchange above them within one Standing, once a year before the contest: one rival, or two from International Standing. The leader rivals the nearest below. They drop rivals that fall out of reach or lose their Exchange.
[*]Old saves: a rival named in 1.0.6 or beta.8 stays your rival. Beta.11 rivalries, which came from diplomacy, no longer count. Diplomatic rivalries are not changed.
[*]Capital fleeing a Financial Panic goes first to a rival Exchange, instead of a diplomatic rival.
[*]The Answer in kind choice of the rival event now names the action and shows its cost and effect.
[/list]
